<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=393" title="View the profile of Zerxes">Zerxes</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 78<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I'm a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=393"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13466#msg13466"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13466#msg13466">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #45 on:</b> December 30, 2004, 12:16:21 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13464#msg13464">Quote from: Karshak on December 30, 2004, 10:54:54 am</a></div><div class="quote">Until those times, can&#039;t you just play WoW quietly? I hope when I quit playing EQ I don&#039;t feel the kind of hatred some of you have for SoE, the game, the timesinks, etc. It would surely make it seem like such an utter waste of time rather than the hobby it started out as.<br /></div><br />I don&#039;t know you Karshak, but I&#039;m assuming you are not (and have never been) a member of a guild that was doing the &quot;leading-edge&quot; content.&nbsp; I can&#039;t speak for Kinny, and I&#039;m not sure he is necessarily an &quot;SoE hater&quot; just because he has openly said he prefers WoW to EQ1, but you need to realize that many of the &quot;SoE haters&quot; are people that were in those kind of guilds, and they have been screwed by SoE in the form of intentional cockblocks, unfinished/bugged content, etc. (again, I&#039;m not sure this applies to Kinaldar so much as it would, say, the &quot;original Ascent&quot;).&nbsp; &nbsp;Contrary to what the poster above said about people will come back to EQ1 or try EQ2, while some may come back, I can assure you that you won&#039;t be seeing guilds like Afterife, Fires of Heaven, etc. coming back to EQ1.&nbsp; They got frustrated at the ineptitude of SoE to the point where they said &quot;enough is enough.&quot;&nbsp; I think it is fair to say these people are more than justified in their &quot;hate&quot; of SoE and in leaving the game.<br /><br />Yes, you are right - WoW involves levelling and getting loot.&nbsp; Yes, raids will require <li type="square"> number of people to log in, although due to instancing it probably won&#039;t require people to schedule their lives around when a mob is expected to spawn (/wave Delheru, I know you hate instancing).&nbsp; The game is a MMORPG after all and so of course its going to share many of the same elements of EQ1.&nbsp; That doesn&#039;t mean, however, they are the same. <br /><br />It will be interesting to see how WoW is doing 1 year from now, as&nbsp; time is the true test of these games.&nbsp; I do know that between beta and the live game, many people have been playing WoW now for over a year, so that&#039;s a pretty good sign of a great game.<br /><br />P.S. For those of you who don&#039;t think EQ is about raiding, I think SoE begs to differ.&nbsp; In distinguishing between EQ and EQ2, SoE has repeatedly said that EQ is much more of a raid oriented game, and will continue to cater to &quot;hard core&quot; raiders, while EQ2 will cater to the more &quot;casual&quot; player crowd, focusing more on solo, group and small raids (18-24 people).&nbsp; Of course, with the mass exodus from the raid game, SoE may change its tune about EQ.<br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13467"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
