	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13472"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=864" title="View the profile of Zorlo">Zorlo</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 50<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=864"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:Zorlo65@yahoo.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13472#msg13472"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13472#msg13472">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #49 on:</b> December 30, 2004, 04:53:19 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Let&#039;s be honest: The game is getting worse, the last two expansions both include like 10 percent of their mobs from Povalor. I play a shaman, and i am flagged and geared to play competently in any grind situation/zone (shh). Typically, shamans and encs and wars and clers are probably the most sought after grouping chars, and i used to have no problem getting a group, even when i wasnt close to as geared as i am now. However, now, it is nearly impossible to find a group. I don&#039;t care how much &quot;nostalgia&quot; you feel about the game, not getting groups is going to kill the game as much as anything. I&#039;m sure i&#039;ll get 300 posts saying, oh Zorlo, you must suck at EQ (possibly) Because i get groups like <i>all</i>  the time. But i know that isnt true, the amount of players has dropped, and the amount of groups have dropped. And when i do get a group, i usually spend it in a Plane of Valor knock off, fighting a Taelosian Rock Formation that looks identical to what i fought in the greatest expansion of all time: PoP. Planes of Power was the high point of EQ imho, the raiding content, while flagging was annoying was awesome, exciting and possible without compromising a fun level of chalenge. The Best guilds got access to the better zones, ie Fire/earth for grinding. Then in GoD, the best guilds got access to KT, the best area for grinding in that expansion. However, in OoW, we have WoS and PG. PG and WoS are arguably the best xp per mob/amount spent in the game atm. However, they have no flags or prequisites. So there is no filter. I know this sounds incredibly pretentious/obnoxious, but the worse players shoudlnt be allowed into the best zones. That was the point of Fire, any grp you got invited into in Fire was competent and well-geared enough to handle the zone, due to the raiding reqs to get in. However, now there is WoS, the new Bastion of Thunder of EQ (you KNOW exactly what i am talking about too) I rarely take groups in Wos, unless i know who is in them, becaus alot of times i end up with lvl 63s, and some people that play casually. I have no problem with that, but they have no buisness in a zone that hits for 2k, and the crs and trains of the zone surely demonstrate my point. At least the mobs in PG are so strong that the avg player wont try to grind there, but unfortunatley some do. <br /><br />In order for EverQuest to survive, and regardless of what you say, it is in a rough time, they need to Lower the raid amounts needed ( in terms of players ), Loosen backflagging, Strengthen flagging, so the good get in, and stay in without having to repeat trivial events, improve the ability of both shms/drus to heal, so there is less dependence on Clerics and figure out a way to start more people joining EQ.<br /><br />Also, this is the rant&#039;s and raves section, I think the &quot;omg, quit ripping EQ/complaining/mathematically proving WoW is better then EQ&quot; comments should stop. Feel free to argue the virtues and vices of the games, but the inherent justification of anyone&#039;s claims on this forum dont need to be proven. Kinladar spent more time experiencing what is the intended purpose of the game then anyone posting; you all should welcome his oppinions, and discuss them, not just flame him for dare speaking ill of EQ, even though he hasnt been anything more then moderate.<br /><br />zorl0<br /><br />P.S.<br /><br />Where did my man Karshak&#039;s post go? I always miss his good ones, did it get deleted? How can something be deleted in a ranting forum? Or did he do it, i dunno.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13473"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=522" title="View the profile of Self Destruction">Self Destruction</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 40<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v425/Undead13/Sharingan.gif" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Sharingan!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=522"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13473#msg13473"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13473#msg13473">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #50 on:</b> December 30, 2004, 05:14:30 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							PG has a pretty good filter as you somewhat mentioned. If you suck, mobs pretty much chew you up and spit you out. Although the zone is really not as hard as some make it seem, if you don&#039;t have your crap together you&#039;re going to be sitting naked at your bind point...and quick.<br /><br />&quot;In order for EverQuest to survive, and regardless of what you say, it is in a rough time, they need to Lower the raid amounts needed ( in terms of players ), Loosen backflagging, Strengthen flagging, so the good get in, and stay in without having to repeat trivial events, improve the ability of both shms/drus to heal, so there is less dependence on Clerics and figure out a way to start more people joining EQ.&quot;<br /><br />agree, agree, agree, etc...<br /><br />&quot; Also, this is the rant&#039;s and raves section, I think the &quot;omg, quit ripping EQ/complaining/mathematically proving WoW is better then EQ&quot; comments should stop.&quot;<br /><br />I&#039;m not sure if this is directed at me (or me and others), but just in case it is, I&#039;ll reply to it...<br /><br />I didn&#039;t flame Kinladar (although I was a touch on the sarcastic side). He asked a question and I answered it. You&#039;re right, it is the Rant and Rave section, but if anything, that only justifies the presence of comments from people saying how tired they are of hearing how super WoW/EQ2 are and in those same posts from people also hearing how much the game we enjoy sucks. Like it or not, this is an EQ &#039;fan&#039; site...term used losely of course.<br /><br />PS. More paragraphs in the first part of your post pls. Not really knocking it, but it would make it easier to read.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><img src="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v425/Undead13/Virsig1.png" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br /><span style="font-family: arial;"><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=859121" target="_blank"><font size="4">Fateseer Virulence</font></a></span><br /><span style="font-family: times;"><font size="3"><b>the Plague 70 Prophet</b><br /></font></span>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13480"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=695" title="View the profile of Larku">Larku</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 9<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=695"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13480#msg13480"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13480#msg13480">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #51 on:</b> December 31, 2004, 08:39:58 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Well. I guess i can say a few words to. I must admit I dont mind hearing about other games, It can be EQ2, WoW or some other game there aint even like EQ. But there have been alot of those posts here where it is more about complaining about EQ, then telling about the other games. And I have no idea where I be will or what i will start to play in the future and I dont really care about right now. I am still having fun in EQ. I have had friends leave for other games, have some there already have returned to EQ, have some there play all 3 of them and have made new friends since the release of EQ2 and WoW.<br /><br />I dont know if I am a &quot;casul&quot; player or not. I must admit becouse of the times i can be on I really never considered raiding much. Also becouse I see EQ for what it is. A game I play for fun, I dont really want it to feal like a Fulltime job and i respect people from both side and really dont care if. I have friends there play less then i do and i have friends there raid almost 24/7 and only play becouse of the raiding they can do. <br /><br />But one thing i must replay to is ( I think Zorlo said it or maybe i misunderstod it) that people there aint in a raiding guild shouldnt be able to be in WoS or PG. Becouse they dont know how to play the game. Well i most admit that most of the times where i have had someone train or &quot;steal&quot; a camp where i was grinding with some friends, have been done by members from some of those tagged players you say know how to play the game and no that wasnt in WoS or PG. and if we shouldnt be allowed in those zones shouldnt raiding guilds keep it members out of the zones where the mobs then dont hit so hard. But yes (to Zorlo again) i agree it is harder to get groups now I hear that more and more to. <br /><br />OK one last thing. SOE have made it easier too backflag now. there is a quest there flags you for Sol ro. So atleast that have been done.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13481"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=236" title="View the profile of Gonaiel">Gonaiel</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 94<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/demon1.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I&#039;m a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=236"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13481#msg13481"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13481#msg13481">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #52 on:</b> December 31, 2004, 12:15:28 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I think what Zorlo means when he says people that don&#039;t belong in certain zones but go there anyhow due to lack not needing a flag or key to get in.&nbsp; Lets use GoD and the sewers and Vixt and tipt as a small example&nbsp; I was a 9500hp tank buffed and good weapons (aggro) I would get beat down pretty fast if I didn&#039;t have a shaman or chanter slow in on him and if I had a cleric that wasn&#039;t on top of the game i would be a dead warriors to.&nbsp; The only thing a tank that has anything less then 9k is good for in those high end zones is loose xp at fast rates and cause long CR runs that would lead to trains and other fun things.&nbsp; The good thing about vixt and tipt is you had to have all the sewers or smith rondo to get in there.&nbsp; You have to know you limits for zones, just becuse you can get to a zone doesn&#039;t mean your ready for it even though the loot is insane.&nbsp; <br /><br />Bot was ruined when they let any person 61 or 62 in with out a flag.&nbsp; That only leads to problems IE trains from mages and chanters KSing for crappy loot.&nbsp; I got so sick of hearing if I ever had to go to BoT &quot;you f-tard you stole my mob and your a kser when were here for 10 hours and you stole our camp and you mom smokes crack&quot;.&nbsp; Where as a zone like Tactics isn&#039;t so bad atleast when i Retired becuse of the flags and random people could just walk in.<br /><br />What makes all of this worse is the lack of CS from GM or guides and when you get KSed or Trained all they would do is say hey that sucks and we cant help you.&nbsp; That is if they responed to you at all.&nbsp; Untill the CS gets better EQ will continue to go down hill.&nbsp; I used to love GM events and untill i retired I didn&#039;t see more then 1 in a span of like 2 or 3 years.&nbsp; I have only seen one time were a GM helped a Raid with a kser other then that you only see sorry but we can help you becuse we cant prove it.<br /><br />For EQ to get better or fix its self so to speak is to...<br />1. get some real Costumer Service and actually tries to help people<br />2. Make certain zones flagged or keyed and is geared for certain players IE. level ablitiy, Gear, Skill by lvl ablitiy&nbsp; I mean like a small quest that you can only do once you hit a certain lvl and make it challaging for a group to do.<br />3. LISTEN AND CARE ABOUT YOUR FAN/PLAYER BASE<br /><br />Those 3 things will start fixing your fan base and bring back the population it was at or close to it.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13482"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=202" title="View the profile of xaanru">xaanru</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 75<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								I&#039;m not a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=202"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13482#msg13482"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13482#msg13482">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #53 on:</b> December 31, 2004, 02:36:40 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I have to chime in on this last discussion. The assumption that having flags, be they for Kod&#039;taz, or PoFire makes you a good player is rather presumptuous.  Honestly, the absolute worst shaman I ever saw, left my guild, went to FoT, and was backflagged thru all the flags up to PoTime. He then accumulated bunches of good gear, and was still a lousy shaman.<br /><br />Being backflagged in a raid of 70 people, does not guarantee that one specific person has ANY talent at all. It just means that the raid leader, and their core people know what they are doing. My very first run through a PoN maze, was with a bunch of Ascent people flagging alts. We had one druid from Forsaken in the raid, and he messed up the whole thing by somehow losing control of his supposedly dire charmed pet, which killed the quest guy while we were fighting the last mob at the end. The entire time wasted, thanks to one &quot;Uber&quot; character.<br /><br />At the time, the threads here were saying Forsaken was one of the top 5 guilds on the server. Sooo, after that guy rode the backs of the core people to some flags, would that really mean that hes suddenly competent?<br /><br />And of course, there is also the inherited/purchased accounts, wherin the new owner may or may not have any talent at that char.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
