	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13483"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=391" title="View the profile of Karshak">Karshak</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 27<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/austin.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I didn&#039;t know that EQ ended.....<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=391"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13483#msg13483"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13483#msg13483">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #54 on:</b> December 31, 2004, 03:23:06 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<i>Why am I quoted in this thread but have no prior post</i> - I deleted my first post here because I figured after writing it that I would be called out by someone as clearly not being hardcore, cutting edge, etc. I was right. I think it&#039;s time to weigh my opinions because I am one of the least represented people here..... the middle of the road hardcore-as-real-life-allows player that enjoys EQ. I am sure I will be torn to shreds, but hey, it will be all last years news tomorrow. :P<br /><br /><i>Why is everything so max/min around here</i> - Soe hasn&#039;t flushed EQ down the shitter Kinladar.... you just stopped enjoying the game as it currently is. Not every player who steps foot into PG without the tag of ascent is a bad player, and conversly not every player who moved from a family guild and got flagged/geared is a waste of space useless player..... what is with the jealousy around here?<br /><br /><i>Am I even eligible to post on anything EQ related</i> - To answer the question about my own eligibility to have a thought I can say that no, I have not being subjected to the woes of the cutting edge guilds. I was not in Fires of Heaven when Furor harbored an erection for his fans to behold and wrote &quot;you have 14 days SoE&quot; on the shaft. I was not in those heady first attacks on unfinished content. On the other hand it has also been a while since I was sitting in dreadlands hoping that no one pulled three mobs by mistake. There are relatively few people who get to attack the cutting edge content. About 24 hours after one guild has done it it ceases to be as difficult for another. Plus, with higher levels, better gear, most in game content is not as difficult. I run with a good guild and enjoy they way they raid. It suits my needs and I hope my online time suits theirs. The content we face is challenging to us and the victories just as exciting.<br /><br /><i>Is the raid leader &gt; the rest of the guild</i> - Guild life is a symbiotic relationship and not just a raid leader with strats in his head shouting at the useless hangers on to do something on his orders. There are few people that can just ride the coat tails to uberfication. I would rather see people just be measured by their ability and be given the relative respect that if the guild is progressing and not using 125 people per event then the sum total of talent/ability/gear of the players is &gt; the target. Usually the weak, useless, players fall by the wayside, quit, or just point fingers at others in a vain hope that they will take the spotlight off themselves.<br /><br /><i>Wow or EQ</i> - I played WoW a little in beta. It was my intention to evaluate it for a long term hobby. I found it had some potential but offered nothing that I am currently finding satisfaction in with EQ. I like to raid. I don&#039;t care if there are strats on the net and I am a loser for not being first. I like guild firsts. I like having guildmates. I have been fortunate to just get accepted to a good guild and intend to enjoy that time as much as possible. I chose not to buy WoW because I haven&#039;t won EQ yet and don&#039;t want to ever put so much time/effort into an online game again. When EQ is done for me, I suspect online gaming will be too.<br /><br /><i>Jerry Springer on a stool</i> - Anyhow, it&#039;s all a game right? Good luck to those of you who go to WoW. Good luck those who stay in EQ1. I will read the boards, hardly ever post, and enjoy EQ for what it is to me, a great, cheap, hobby that provides me with hours of amusement and new people to meet in a submersive world. It&#039;s what you make it, but make it for yourself, and if you hate it now I don&#039;t have to do I?<br /><br />Happy New Year to all. 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
