					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13485"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=864" title="View the profile of Zorlo">Zorlo</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 50<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=864"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:Zorlo65@yahoo.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13485#msg13485"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13485#msg13485">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #56 on:</b> December 31, 2004, 10:59:36 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Several things,<br /><br />I thought about what you said, that Rants and Raves justifies both what i meant and what i didnt and you are right, so i suppose what i was saying was that: Kinladar isnt inherently evil because he is objective/negative about the future of EQ.<br /><br />Also: Thank you very much for pointing out that not all flagged people are competent, obviously, i represent that :P . And likewise, not all un-flagged people are incompetent. I am just saying that the people in raid guilds, typically have invested the time to learn their class enough to function better in more difficult zones, that should only be open to them. <br /><br />Also: If you let everyone into every zone (thank you, i realize not every zone) and give them incredible loots (I realize, there is better loot in flagged zones) you take alot of the reward out of playing at the higher end. For example, a 63 rogue w/ 2aa gets into a PG grp with some friends, wins a roll on some item with 130hp/mana, etc, while getting insane xp for his level. Or a 70 cleric with 250aa, gets an item on a Time raid with 130hp/mana. We all know that time is old, and alot have passed it, but let&#039;s face it, the quality of loot off of trashmobs in PG is almost Time p1 quality. We also know that is easiest to succeed in Eles, by fighting in VT, easiest to win in Time from farming Eles, easiest to progress through GoD by killing Quarm, easiest to break into Anguish by killing Qvic/Txevu/Tacvi. That is the way the game is supposed to be played raid-wise, and players should be rewarded with gear based on the level of their content and access to zones. If a 59 war can get 120hp stuff in WoS, and a 70 war&#039;s guild barely kills Agnarr, where is the incentive for new guilds to progress? There is none. Why fight in the Eles? When we get better gear from PG? Oh right, because we have to get to Time. <br /><br />That is fairly verbose, but the point is this: The Majority of players in raiding Guilds around 10-5 (OA, BM, IL, Apoth, UoP) are forced to raid content that is irrelevant gear wise to acces relevant goals, essentially wasting their time, a time waster that forces players out of guilds that want to move faster, thus crippling guilds. <br /><br />Additionally, higher end guilds (RoS, Conv, Ascent, Da/EiE) are reaching new content and new gear, but no new grinding zones. They have access to the same zones about 80 percent of the server does. I have no problem with them getting a &quot;uber xp&quot; zone that only the best can get into, they deserve it. However, they are stuck in the BoT of OoW: WoS/PG. For players who take this game as seriously, they deserve the best zones.<br /><br />I thought about it, and no, it isnt elitist to give the best players the best zones, they are entitled to it more then people who play once a month for two reasons. One, they need it more, and two, this game is based on progression (levels, gear, aa) if you are willing to give every player access to the best zones to grind in, and top of the line gear, why not give everyone 200aa, and get them to 70 with 10k unbuffed. <br /><br />Zorlo
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
