	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13495"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1" title="View the profile of Kinladar">Kinladar</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Ranger Bait<br />
								Administrator<br />
								Veeshan<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 14456<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/macross.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								My Avatar can beat up your avatar!<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kinladar@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kinladar@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org" title="http://www.rodcetnife.org" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:truman@thewavz.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13495#msg13495"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13495#msg13495">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #58 on:</b> January 02, 2005, 01:33:11 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							If you wanna use the bazaar as an indicator, not long ago they had to increase the max number of vendors in the bazaar to over the initial 500 limit, due to it maxing out so often.<br /><br />A few months after GoD release, you&#039;d see the bazaar around 300-400 people, cause alot of people had already quit with the debacle that was GoD.<br /><br />If it&#039;s now down to 200 or so, then to use th bazaar crowd as an indicator of population, that is a 3/5 decline or about that in overall population in the last year or so.<br /><br />Why is this?<br /><br />EQ got boring in many people&#039;s opinions. That&#039;s happened with alot of my Casual, and Hardcore friends, in reality, EQ started loosing the up and coming crowd with how much work it took to get to max levels for raiding guilds.<br /><br />70 levels, and typically 150+ AA, not much in some circles, but more work than alot of them wanted to commit.<br /><br />If you had no one to PL you through the levels, you are talking a ton of time investment, and still no garauntee you&#039;d make it in.<br /><br />Mudflation finally did what no other game had been able to do. By making players more and more powerfull in the build ups for thier toons, they built in the increasing difficulty of a new player to have a chance to &quot;catch up.&quot;<br /><br />Some people like to state that we shouldn&#039;t be telling SoE what to do, that they were the ones with the empire of 500K accounts etc etc etc....<br /><br />Well, I take the opposite side, in that they grew arrogant, and forgot where they came from in the old school game, because it was the old game that attracted 500K players, and not the mess it is today.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.wowrankings.com/viewb.htm?name=Kinladar&amp;s_id=38" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/sig-kinladar-wow.jpg" alt="" border="0" /></a><br /><a href="http://www.chaoticdiscord.org" target="_blank">Chaotic Discord</a> found in {World of Warcraft}<br />Guild Leader of Fires of Time (Retired)
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13497"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=665" title="View the profile of Naithein">Naithein</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 135<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/44-knightman.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Rawr ?<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/laldayen@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="laldayen@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://edit.yahoo.com/config/send_webmesg?.target=naithein%40yahoo.com"><img src="http://opi.yahoo.com/online?u=naithein%40yahoo.com&amp;m=g&amp;t=0" alt="naithein@yahoo.com" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="aim:goim?screenname=PadisharrCreel&amp;message=Hi.+Are+you+there?"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/aim.gif" alt="PadisharrCreel" border="0" /></a><br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=665"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.xanga.com/lamdeir" title="" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:laldayen@hotmail.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13497#msg13497"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13497#msg13497">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #59 on:</b> January 02, 2005, 02:47:04 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13495#msg13495">Quote from: Kinladar on January 02, 2005, 01:33:11 pm</a></div><div class="quote">70 levels, and typically 150+ AA, not much in some circles, but more work than alot of them wanted to commit.<br /><br />If you had no one to PL you through the levels, you are talking a ton of time investment, and still no garauntee you&#039;d make it in.<br /><br />Mudflation finally did what no other game had been able to do. By making players more and more powerfull in the build ups for thier toons, they built in the increasing difficulty of a new player to have a chance to &quot;catch up.&quot;<br /><br />Some people like to state that we shouldn&#039;t be telling SoE what to do, that they were the ones with the empire of 500K accounts etc etc etc....<br /><br />Well, I take the opposite side, in that they grew arrogant, and forgot where they came from in the old school game, because it was the old game that attracted 500K players, and not the mess it is today.<br /></div><br />/Much agreed. <br /><br />Part of the fallout is credited to Sony&#039;s lack of ability to create new worlds and keep players interested. (i.e., when Planes of Power was first released, it wasn&#039;t even fully completed.) Verant did a good job in that - they made new dungeons and new worlds for people to explore and it was exciting all at once, but SoE -at least imo, has become too predictable, and it&#039;s the same thing over again. <br />What did level 70 give us? Some more HP and a Few spells, that&#039;s pretty much it. Sure the AA were nifty but by the time they were done inputting all the AA&quot;s etc, people were tired of Grinding for them for the same mediocre rewards as before.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />[56 Paladin] Naithein (High Elf) - Rodcet Nife <br />[54 Druid] Naithien (Wood Elf) - Rodcet Nife<br />[43 Monk] Spankii (Human) - Rodcet Nife
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
